# Line ending normalization — IMPORTANT for WSL2 environments
# After modifying this file, always run: git add --renormalize .
# Without renormalization, git rewrites files during checkout to convert
# line endings, which can corrupt WSL2 inodes (symptoms: ??????? permissions,
# ENOENT on files that exist). See session log 2026-02-08_20-35-05 for details.
#
# Normalize line endings to LF on commit
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly declare text files
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Windows batch launcher: must keep CRLF bytes IN THE BLOB. install.ps1 downloads
# the raw blob directly from raw.githubusercontent.com, so `eol=crlf` (which stores
# a normalized LF blob and only converts on checkout) would NOT give the downloaded
# copy CRLF. `-text` disables normalization entirely, preserving the committed CRLF.
*.bat -text

# Binary files (don't modify)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.parquet binary
